# McNdroid

**A Longitudinal Multimodal Benchmark for Robust Drift Detection in Android Malware**

[![Paper](https://img.shields.io/badge/arXiv-2605.06894-b31b1b.svg)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06894)
[![Dataset](https://img.shields.io/badge/Hugging%20Face-McNdroid-FFD21E)](https://huggingface.co/datasets/IQSeC-Lab/McNdroid)
[![Zenodo](https://img.shields.io/badge/Zenodo-Dataset-1682D4)](https://zenodo.org/records/19969833)
[![Dataset License](https://img.shields.io/badge/Dataset%20License-CC%20BY%204.0-lightgrey.svg)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)

McNdroid is a large-scale, longitudinal, multimodal benchmark for studying Android malware detection under temporal distribution shift. It contains **858,859 applications** spanning **2013–2025, excluding 2015**, with **1,354 malware families** and three hash-aligned feature modalities:

* **Static:** DREBIN-style features extracted from Android manifests and smali code.
* **Dynamic:** behavioral features derived from sandbox execution reports.
* **Graph:** structural features derived from function-call graphs represented in GML.

The repository provides preprocessing utilities, official temporal splits, unimodal and multimodal baselines, drift analyses, concept-drift adaptation, continual-learning experiments, missing-modality evaluation, feature-importance analysis, and cross-modal disagreement measurements.

> **Dataset:** [Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/datasets/IQSeC-Lab/McNdroid) | [Zenodo](https://zenodo.org/records/19969833)
> **Paper:** [arXiv:2605.06894](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06894)

