## Benchmark Overview

| Property         | Description                                                         |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Domain           | Android malware detection                                           |
| Samples          | 858,859 applications                                                |
| Time span        | 2013–2025, excluding 2015                                           |
| Malware families | 1,354                                                               |
| Modalities       | Static, dynamic, and graph-based features                           |
| Alignment        | Modalities are aligned by application hash and binary label         |
| Labels           | Binary malware/benign labels and multi-vendor family verdicts       |
| Dataset size     | Approximately 10.9 GB                                               |
| Primary setting  | Train on historical data and evaluate on chronologically later data |
| Dataset license  | Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International                      |

### Supported Research Tasks

McNdroid supports research on:

* temporal generalization and concept drift;
* unimodal and multimodal Android malware detection;
* early, late, and attention-based feature fusion;
* concept-drift detection and budget-constrained adaptation;
* domain-incremental and class-incremental continual learning;
* cross-modal agreement and modality dissent;
* feature-space drift, feature stability, and temporal explainability;
* robustness to missing modalities and partial feature masking;
* malware-family evolution, label drift, and uncertainty analysis; and
* graph-based malware classification.

---

## Repository Structure

| Directory                                                | Purpose                                                                                              |
| -------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| [`preprocessing/`](preprocessing/)                       | Builds static, graph, and dynamic feature representations and constructs train/test splits.          |
| [`splits/`](splits/)                                     | Official year-specific split definitions for 2013, 2014, and 2016–2025.                              |
| [`concept_drift/`](concept_drift/)                       | Unimodal and multimodal temporal generalization experiments.                                         |
| [`concept-drift-adaptation/`](concept-drift-adaptation/) | Month-wise CADE and hierarchical contrastive-learning adaptation experiments under labeling budgets. |
| [`continual-learning/`](continual-learning/)             | Domain-incremental and class-incremental continual-learning experiments.                             |
| [`distribution-shift/`](distribution-shift/)             | Statistical distribution-shift measurement using two-sample Kolmogorov–Smirnov tests.                |
| [`feature-importance/`](feature-importance/)             | SHAP-based temporal feature and feature-group importance analysis.                                   |
| [`feature-space-aio-umap/`](feature-space-aio-umap/)     | UMAP-based visualization of feature-space drift.                                                     |
| [`feature-stability/`](feature-stability/)               | Temporal feature divergence and malware-family stability analysis.                                   |
| [`missing-feature/`](missing-feature/)                   | Robustness evaluation under missing modalities and random feature masking.                           |
| [`uncertainity-label-drift/`](uncertainity-label-drift/) | Prediction-uncertainty experiments under benign-to-malware and malware-to-benign label drift.        |
| [`x-modality-disagreement/`](x-modality-disagreement/)   | Cross-modal disagreement, prediction logging, and modality-dissenter analysis.                       |
| [`mcn_metadata.json`](mcn_metadata.json)                 | Machine-readable Croissant dataset metadata.                                                         |

Each experimental directory contains a module-specific README or executable scripts with the relevant arguments and output conventions.

